ROW2["`💰 …and in the AI path, where the money actually goes`"]
  K4["`4 · OLLAMA LAST IN THE CHAIN
one piece, THREE problems:
· no total outage from a vendor failure
· no lock-in — none is irreplaceable
· zero API cost in dev and CI`"]
ROW2 -.- K4
  K6["`6 · THE PLANNER KNOWS IT IS EXPENSIVE
code checks always (free)
LLM judge ONLY when flagged
or the context came back weak
clean plan = 1 call · worst case 3`"]
  K7["`7 · IT METERS ITSELF
the part most systems skip
provider returns Completion(text, model,
TokenUsage), not a string: the SAME plan
costs 0.5¢ or 30¢ depending which model
answered — a string cannot say which
UsageLedger sums planner + repair +
judge + one call per item`"]
  K4 -.- K6 -.- K7 -.- K8
  K8["`BUDGET — checked AT THE DOOR,
once per plan, never mid-run
stopping halfway spends the tokens
and delivers a half-written plan
overshoot bounded by one plan = cents
calendar month UTC: 'it resets on the first'
is a sentence a person can act on`"]

ROW1["`💰 WHERE CHEAP AND CORRECT AGREED — infrastructure`"]
  K1["`1 · LOCAL EMBEDDINGS — bge-m3 on Ollama
